1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,378
AIRadio streams internet radio..

2
00:00:03,328 --> 00:00:10,054
To keep audio playing in the background, it
uses a foreground service of type media playback..

3
00:00:10,054 --> 00:00:17,391
Tapping a station makes PlayerViewModel dispatch
an ACTION_PLAY intent to startForegroundService..

4
00:00:17,391 --> 00:00:27,024
The manifest declares foreground service type media playback
and the matching FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK permission..

5
00:00:27,024 --> 00:00:36,277
RadioPlayerService calls ServiceCompat startForeground
with FOREGROUND_SERVICE_TYPE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK..

6
00:00:36,277 --> 00:00:42,961
It holds a partial wake lock and a Wi-Fi lock,
so the stream survives the screen turning off..

7
00:00:42,961 --> 00:00:50,801
A media-style notification shows the station
name, country, and Play, Pause, and Stop actions..

8
00:00:50,801 --> 00:01:00,584
The same surface appears on the lock screen and in system media
controls, because the service registers an AndroidX Media3 MediaSession..

9
00:01:00,584 --> 00:01:05,298
When the user presses Home, AIRadio moves to background..

10
00:01:05,298 --> 00:01:09,171
Audio focus is still held by AIRadio..

11
00:01:09,171 --> 00:01:13,546
The service stays foreground, and the radio keeps playing..

12
00:01:13,546 --> 00:01:18,369
This is exactly what the mediaPlayback foreground service is for..

13
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:22,432
Tapping Stop runs stopForeground and stopSelf..

14
00:01:22,432 --> 00:01:28,383
The notification disappears, the service
ends, and audio focus is released..

